{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/mac/window_channel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:36:01.868553Z","id":"15451942eb811a1110fbf151392f80123b3d6a20d9e497b837d3c70f94ea2cd2","body":{"detail":"_wanting and _wantedSent are static and setEscapeWanted is a no-op without hasDesktopWindowChrome. test/ui/app_screen_test.dart's pane and popover tests close what they opened before ending for this reason; without that, 'on macOS the window is told Escape is wanted…' later in the file sees no setEscapeWanted call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"2400eff3966a96ea4945af61ed185d94fa3cb385490f53ab1ce2d9e08ee07c38"},"suggested_fix":"Give MacWindow a @visibleForTesting reset() (as MacToolbar has) and call it in the tests' set-up.","summary":"A macOS-variant widget test that ends with comment mode, the panel or a composer up leaves MacWindow's Escape state behind for the next test: the variant puts the platform back before the tree is torn down, so AppScreen.dispose's setEscapeWanted(false) returns early","tags":["tests","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
